        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor: use native abort signal composition",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw carried several private abort-signal combinators with separate listener cleanup and unsupported-runtime fallback logic, despite requiring Node 22.19+ where `AbortSignal.any` is available. The duplication made first-abort reason propagation and cleanup behavior harder to audit across agents, media, ACP, and plugins.\n\nRelated: #105907\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Replace private composition helpers and manual abort relays with native `AbortSignal.any` at their owning call sites.\n- Remove obsolete fallback implementations and fallback-only tests.\n- Preserve optional/single-signal behavior and first-abort reasons.\n- Keep Discord's shipped `mergeAbortSignals` runtime export as a thin compatibility wrapper while migrating internal callers off it.\n- Leave retry, timeout-wrapper, reconnect, and backoff consolidation to separate PRs.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo intended user-visible behavior change. Abort propagation keeps existing ordering, reasons, timeout logging, and response-body cancellation semantics with less custom code.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Production LOC: `+63/-300` (net `-237`); total diff: `+106/-509` (net `-403`).\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxcreacpxyysfyvqv2y69w8n`: 13 focused Vitest shards passed across core, agents, ACP, auto-reply, media, Discord, Slack, Signal, and opencode-go.\n- The focused suite's first cold run hit an existing 1-second ACP startup wait at 1.012s; the isolated warm rerun passed at 530ms and the complete rerun passed at 332ms.\n- `pnpm check:changed` passed formatting, four tsgo lanes, core/extension lint, import-cycle, storage, and repository guards before the final unrelated main rebase.\n- Exact-head `check:changed` now stops at pre-existing TypeScript LOC baseline growth on untouched main files. This PR's `message-media.ts` growth was reduced to zero; all touched large files now match or shrink their baselines.\n- Fresh branch autoreview: no findings; patch correct at 0.93 confidence.\n- No changelog: internal refactor with no intended user-visible change.\n",
